Module 9: Clocking and Power

Purpose:
- Provide low jitter clocks for ADC and FPGA and stable power rails for analog and digital sections.

Clock tree:
- Primary: Si5341 or Si570 low jitter oscillator configured to output ADC_CLK (250 MHz LVDS) and FPGA reference clocks (125/250 MHz as needed).
- Backup: 25 MHz crystal + PLL if cheaper option selected; ensure jitter within ADC spec.

Power rails (examples):
- AVDD (ADC analog): 3.3V LDO (low noise) with ferrite bead separation
- VREF: 2.5V external precision reference (REF5025/ADR4525) buffered as required
- FPGA core: 1.0V/1.2V switching regulator + LDO post regulation
- Digital I/O: 1.8V / 3.3V rails via LDOs; decoupling 0.1uF + 10nF + 1uF per pin group

Protection and sequencing:
- Provide power-on sequencing if ADC/FPGA require specific order; use supervisor ICs for reset generation.

Verification:
- Measure clock jitter with spectrum analyzer; verify rail noise with scope and check ADC performance vs jitter.
